 that in terms of a book, not many folk recognise the 'Vampire Diary: the Embrace'. I bought it new when it first came out and I'd love to use it as a prop one day.<br /> Besides that I have a full set of Jyhad cards (the first set).<br /> <br /> All part of one of my favourite game systems.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-12-14T13:26:28-08:00","id":340189,"title":"","content":"All of you guys with OWoD Clan Pins make me exceptionally sad that I wasn't into Masquerade while they were a thing. Or rather, wasn't into LARP version of Masquerade while they were a thing (I'd kill for Toreador, Camarilla, Anarch and Nosferatu pins). I do have some other swag from NWoD though...<br /> <br /> * Two copies of Book of Nod (couldn't pass them up in a game store, brand new, for $4 on the 'used' shelf)<br /> * Rites of the Dragon (NWoD prop book for Ordo Dracul)<br /> * NWoD Forsaken Dogtag - Rahu<br /> * NWoD Requiem Clan Pins - Daeva, Gangrel<br /> * NWoD Requiem Covenant Pins - Ordo Dracul, Invictus, Sanctified","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-01-16T15:46:14-08:00","id":810388,"title":"","content":"Just got this today. Werewolf the Apocalypse logo. Does it count as swag?<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://41.media.tumblr.com/a5668ef7e91de0ddfedc31654dfda392/tumblr_o12hsbuc3W1rswd31o1_1280.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" a